arch questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature (test coverage). Low complexity. Additive test only. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A single integration test writes a plan containing at least one T0 bookend task and one TN bookend task via the SAM plan writer\\n- The test reads the written file back via the SAM plan reader\\n- Field-level equality asserted on all bookend-specific fields: `is_bookend`, `bookend_type`, `acceptance_criteria_structured`\\n- Test uses `tmp_path` pytest fixture for isolation (no real filesystem side effects)\\n- Test passes with the current implementation and catches any future serialization regression\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sam_bookend_roundtrip.py` \u2014 new integration test file\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a SAM bookend implementer, I need a round-trip integration test that writes a plan with bookend fields via the writer and reads it back via the reader so serialization/deserialization bugs in bookend-specific fields are caught before they reach production.\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P697-sam-bookend-validation-followup-2.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:35:42Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7ceb8cf376211ed974c00112dce99bfee5e6d10a5347023c6fb0a414be8a62ca\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgzEcA\"}"}